Proposed (27.3s): Use this skill whenever the user is about to build, design, plan, rethink, or sanity-check anything measurement-shaped — a dashboard, KPI, metric, scorecard, leaderboard, ranking, report, or analytics screen that scores people, teams, or channels. Trigger on intent, not keywords: "which KPIs belong here," "how should we measure X productivity," "rethink what's on this leaderboard," "this screen feels too simple, replan it," "any concerns before I build this dashboard," "what do we measure and how do we lay it out," "is this metric fair." The shared signal is someone deciding WHAT to measure and HOW to show it before writing queries — especially when fairness, gaming, attribution, or "does this drive a decision" is at stake. Run a rigorous senior-PM brainstorm: tear down vanity/gameable/mislabeled/confounded metrics, split scores from context, fix attribution, lock each choice before building. Skip only for pure execution with no design judgment (write this SQL, fix a chart axis, translate labels, schedule an existing report).

